$\frac{1}{2}=\frac{4}{8}$ and $\frac{1}{4}=\frac{2}{8}$.
Label $4$ sectors A and $2$ sectors B. The remaining $8-4-2=2$ sectors are C.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) circle (1.8);
\foreach \k in {0,...,7} {\draw[black] (0,0) -- ({90-45*\k}:1.8);}
\foreach \angle/\label in {67.5/A,22.5/A,-22.5/A,-67.5/A,-112.5/B,-157.5/B,-202.5/C,-247.5/C} {\path (\angle:1.25) node {\label};}
\fill[black] (0,0) circle (0.05);
\draw[black,thick,->] (0,0) -- (90:1.55);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The probability of C is $\frac{2}{8}=\frac{1}{4}$.
The counts total $4+2+2=8$.
